<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The Mac App Store edition's entitlements (PLAN_MAS_FORK §3, 2026-10-30).
  Referenced ONLY by tauri.appstore.conf.json — the direct channel
  (Developer ID DMG) signs with NO entitlements, deliberately: the store
  edition is the sandboxed one.

  The set is the plan's sanctioned v1 exactly:
    app-sandbox          — the store's hard requirement; the kernel's data
                           root (app_data_dir()/kernel) is container-
                           redirected by construction, so nothing relocates
    network.server       — the sidecar kernel LISTENS on 127.0.0.1:8765;
                           this is also what lets the openclaw host AND a
                           user-installed signal-gateway connect from outside
    network.client       — the webview's fetches to the loopback kernel, the
                           model fetch, and the gateway DETECT probe
    application-identifier / team-identifier — the store's signing identity

  Deliberately ABSENT (named, not hidden — PLAN_MAS_FORK §6 carries them as
  open questions): keychain-access-groups (the default app group is drilled
  at Phase 0), the private-cloud-compute entitlement (requested in the ASC
  record; NOT GRANTED as of 2026-11-03 — the App ID is registered WITHOUT
  the FoundationModels capability, so the store edition generates
  on-device-only and .deep stays nominal; when granted, enabling the
  capability on the App ID and regenerating the profile flips the tier with
  zero code changes — the probe-first law), and the 27-era
  hardened-process enhanced-security-version (measured, not assumed, before
  it ships). The provisionprofile is injected by the MAS lane's generated
  overlay — never committed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
	<string>JHB4UNPL3G.com.stewardmem.shell.mas</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
	<string>JHB4UNPL3G</string>
</dict>
</plist>
